From 4b876b2a336f8db800ce8fc833f303386dbddf40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:58:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(journal): add free-text search to Journal Entries
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Journal Entries could only be filtered by type (Auto/Manual) and a
date range — finding one specific entry meant scrolling through the
list by eye. Adds a search box above those filters that matches, on
the server:

- the voucher number (reference_code)
- the entry's own narration
- any line's own narration
- the line's account name or code
- the line's Sub Ledger (business partner) name or code
- an exact debit/credit amount, when the search text is a plain
  number (commas allowed, e.g. "20,000")

Search is debounced 300ms client-side before it's sent, so typing
doesn't fire a request per keystroke. The empty-state message now
says what search term came up empty, instead of a generic "No
entries found."

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TzRYcGBjDHGFFNgpNih7vR
